            <ArticleTitle>[Misdiagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea hypopnea syndrome].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>418-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To enhance the understanding of obstructive sleep apnea hypopnea syndrome (OSAHS) and lower its misdiagnosis.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">6 misdiagnosed cases were analyzed systemically.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">OSAHS can be misdiagnosed as primary hypertension, arrhythmia, asthma, acalcerosis and some other diseases. The main causes of misdiagnosis were: the main complaints and the main signs could be one or more of a series of symptoms or signs of OSAHS itself or its complications and the lack of systemic knowledge of OSAHS.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The understanding of OSAHS could be enhanced by analyzing misdiagnosis cases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
